{"id":"nave:goat","source":"nave","name":"Goat","slug":"goat","seeAlso":[],"entries":[{"text":"Designated as one of the ceremonially clean animals to be eaten De 14:4; with Le 11:1-8","refs":[["Deut",14,4,14,4],["Lev",11,1,11,8]]},{"text":"Used for food Ge 27:9; 1Sa 16:20","refs":[["Gen",27,9,27,9],["1Sam",16,20,16,20]]},{"text":"For the paschal feast Ex 12:5; 2Ch 35:7","refs":[["Exod",12,5,12,5],["2Chr",35,7,35,7]]},{"text":"As a sacrifice by Abraham Ge 15:9","refs":[["Gen",15,9,15,9]]},{"text":"By Gideon Jud 6:19","refs":[["Judg",6,19,6,19]]},{"text":"Manoah Jud 13:19","refs":[["Judg",13,19,13,19]]},{"text":"Milk of, used for food Pr 27:27","refs":[["Prov",27,27,27,27]]},{"text":"Hair of, used for clothing Nu 31:20","refs":[["Num",31,20,31,20]]},{"text":"Pillows 1Sa 19:13","refs":[["1Sam",19,13,19,13]]},{"text":"Curtains of the tabernacle Ex 26:7; 35:23; 36:14","refs":[["Exod",26,7,26,7],["Exod",35,23,35,23],["Exod",36,14,36,14]]},{"text":"Regulations of Mosaic law required that a baby goat should not be killed for food before it was eight days old Le 22:27","refs":[["Lev",22,27,22,27]]},{"text":"Nor seethed in its mother’s milk Ex 23:19","refs":[["Exod",23,19,23,19]]},{"text":"Numerous De 32:14; So 4:1; 6:5; 1Sa 25:2; 2Ch 17:11","refs":[["Deut",32,14,32,14],["Song",4,1,4,1],["Song",6,5,6,5],["1Sam",25,2,25,2],["2Chr",17,11,17,11]]},{"text":"Wild, in Palestine 1Sa 24:2; Ps 104:18","refs":[["1Sam",24,2,24,2],["Ps",104,18,104,18]]}],"refCount":24}
